    "updated_at": "2026-11-25T10:54:23Z",
    "body": "Closing the other two in favor of this one, and will add comments there.\n\nRelevant context:\n\nFrom #2562:\n- Chromium's original tracking bug for ignoring cross-origin download: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=714373\nThis applies when there is no `Content-Disposition: attachment` header on the response.\n\nFrom #7718:\n- Link to #5548 (Should downloads be \"navigate\" or \"no-cors\") — fixing this may tie into unifying downloads with the navigation algorithm.\n\n- @domenic's note on <a download href=\"#foo\"> (Chrome tries to download, Firefox navigates).",
